For recurring task-620c4650, transform an HxW input into a 3H x 2W output. Let A be the input rotated 180 degrees. Make three vertical blocks in order A, vertical-flip(A), A. In each output row, append the row's left-right reversal horizontally, so the two horizontal blocks are row and its mirror. Equivalently, tile A, its vertical flip, and A vertically, with each tile mirrored on the right. Dimensions are 3H by 2W; preserve all colors exactly.

Confirmed demonstrations/tests: input 10x5 -> output 30x10; the top-left block is input rotated 180°, top-right is its horizontal reflection, middle block is vertical reflection of the top, and bottom repeats top. A separate test input 8x4 was solved correctly as 24x8. This instance's 2x10 test was solved correctly without demos: input [[0,0,9,3,4,0,0,0,0,6],[0,3,8,0,6,9,0,4,0,0]] gives the following 6x20 output, confirming the construction: [[0,0,4,0,9,6,0,8,3,0,0,3,8,0,6,9,0,4,0,0],[6,0,0,0,0,4,3,9,0,0,0,0,9,3,4,0,0,0,0,6],[6,0,0,0,0,4,3,9,0,0,0,0,9,3,4,0,0,0,0,6],[0,0,4,0,9,6,0,8,3,0,0,3,8,0,6,9,0,4,0,0],[0,0,4,0,9,6,0,8,3,0,0,3,8,0,6,9,0,4,0,0],[6,0,0,0,0,4,3,9,0,0,0,0,9,3,4,0,0,0,0,6]]. Both solved with no incorrect submissions; one earlier instance used one demo.
